provenance probe java=55ff8a4ec7e186d9816cd549246b4cf1f59c9f12 datapack=55ff8a4ec7e186d9816cd549246b4cf1f59c9f12
note Each row runs a fresh script (and a second one, B, where named) on probe NPCs npc1, npc2 and players p1, p2. Lines: every start with its result, then every firing (at is the virtual time since the row began) and every cancel, in order. Timers due at the same time fire in start order (the probe's thread pool; the reference pool does not order ties).
note A one-shot timer leaves the set before its hook runs: the hook sees no pending timer under its own key and may start the same key again.
row removed-before-hook
  start A probe npc=npc1 player=p1 delay=1000 -> true
  fire A probe npc=npc1 player=p1 at=1000
    pending-in-hook=false
  start A probe npc=npc1 player=p1 delay=1000 -> true
  fire A probe npc=npc1 player=p1 at=2000
    pending-in-hook=false
row restart-in-hook
  start A rearm npc=npc1 player=none delay=1000 -> true
  fire A rearm npc=npc1 player=none at=1000
    pending-in-hook=false
    restart rearm -> true
  fire A rearm npc=npc1 player=none at=2000
    pending-in-hook=false
row zero-delay
  start A now npc=none player=p1 delay=0 -> true
  fire A now npc=none player=p1 at=0

