note Each row runs a fresh script (and a second one, B, where named) on probe NPCs npc1, npc2 and players p1, p2. Lines: every start with its result, then every firing (at is the virtual time since the row began) and every cancel, in order. Timers due at the same time fire in start order (the probe's thread pool; the reference pool does not order ties).
note startQuestTimerAtFixedRate(name, npc, player, initial, period): fires at initial, then every period on a fixed grid; it stays in the set (a restart is refused) until cancelled.
row grid
  start A tick npc=none player=p1 initial=1000 period=500 -> true
  fire A tick npc=none player=p1 at=1000
  fire A tick npc=none player=p1 at=1500
  fire A tick npc=none player=p1 at=2000
  start A tick npc=none player=p1 delay=100 -> false
  fire A tick npc=none player=p1 at=2500
  cancel tick npc=none player=p1

